> (1) mixed logit models like yours are not fit using REML. The default 
> fit uses Laplace approximation, which apparently is related to, but not 
> the same as REML.

Yes, true, thanks for the correction.  In fact, if I now recall 
correctly, lme4 always uses Laplace-approximated maximum-likelihood 
estimation for logit models (is this right?).

